{
 "regions": [
  {
   "id": "r2",
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "that they are—rejoice when on the contrary they ought",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "to grieve ! !",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r3",
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "60. The clod of earth is encircled by the watery edge.",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "Even when taken as a whole, it is indeed very small; and it",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "is apportioned by a number of kings and enjoyed after",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "hundreds of battles. Abject and exceedingly poor, they",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "therefore, give or would give nothing. Fie upon those",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "mean fellows who wish to get even from them a piece of coin.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r4",
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "61. He (lit. that singularly fortunate person) alone was",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "born whose white skull was, by the enemy of the god of",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "love, held prominently on his head as an ornament; ( and",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "yet ) what height of morbid presumption is there on the part",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "of men when a few persons solicitous of saving their own",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "lives bow to them.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r5",
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "62. Alas ! ( my ) heart, why dost thou enter the dense",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "mass of misery ( suffer much distress ) in order to please the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "hearts of others by daily propitiation ? when with the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "powers of the Chintámani spontaneously rising in thee, thou",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "art inwardly satisfied, what object of thine foregone-desire",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "will not satisfy ?",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r6",
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "63. Why do you wander for nothing, oh mind ? Rest",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "yourself somewhere. A thing that naturally ( lit. of itself )",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "takes a particular course does take it; it changes not.",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "Without, therefore, remembering what is past, or speculating",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "about what is to come, do you in this world experience",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "fruits, the coming and going of which cannot be determined",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 7,
     "text": "beforehand.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r7",
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "64. Now be pleased, O heart; cease from these trouble-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "some abyss of sensual objects; resort to the path of final bea-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "titude which is capable of removing, in a moment, all misery;",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "assume a peaceful attitude, give up your course unsteady",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "like a wave and never again be attached to transient worldly",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "happiness.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r1",
   "type": "page_number",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "[ 37 ]",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  }
 ],
